#: docs/user-guide/concepts/behavior-groups.md:78
msgid "_For language implementers._ Groups are authoring metadata on the authored system (`BehaviorGroup { scope, name, members }`), never read by flattening or any analysis; the formal development proves every kernel judgment is that of the ungrouped design (ADR-0019, `docs/evidence/behavior-systems-correspondence.md` Phase 8b). The boundary (crossing-in, crossing-out, open, driven, private) is a projection of the dependency graph, and an aggregate socket adds no dependency edge."
