msgstr "1.89 — リポジトリで固定、`rustup` でインストール"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:11
msgid "builds the compiler service, and the firmware for a board (the board's target, `thumbv6m-none-eabi` for the Raspberry Pi Pico, is installed by `rustup` the first time a build needs it)"
msgstr "コンパイラサービスと、ボード向けファームウェアをビルドします（ボードのターゲット——Raspberry Pi Pico なら `thumbv6m-none-eabi`——は最初のビルドが必要とした時に `rustup` がインストールします）"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:12
msgid "Flutter"
msgstr "Flutter"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:12
msgid "3.47"
msgstr "3.47"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:12
msgid "builds Studio; on macOS, `brew install --cask flutter`"
msgstr "Studio をビルドする。macOS では `brew install --cask flutter`"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:13
msgid "`just`"
msgstr "`just`"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:13
msgid "the task runner the repository uses"
msgstr "リポジトリが使うタスクランナー"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:15
msgid "macOS and Windows are the supported desktops. Linux builds as a by-product but is not exercised."
msgstr "サポートされるデスクトップは macOS と Windows です。Linux は副産物としてビルドできますが、検証されていません。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:18
msgid "Build and run"
msgstr "ビルドと実行"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:20
msgid "From the repository root:"
msgstr "リポジトリのルートで："

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:26
msgid "This builds `bdld` and starts Studio pointed at it. The first build takes several minutes; later ones are quick."
msgstr "これで `bdld` をビルドし、それを指す Studio を起動します。最初のビルドには数分かかりますが、その後は速くなります。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:29
msgid "**Run it from Terminal or a Finder-launched shell**, not from a terminal embedded in another application. macOS refuses to show file dialogs to apps launched from sandboxed hosts; Studio detects that and offers typed paths instead (_Open by path…_, _New at path…_), but the native dialogs are the intended way."
msgstr "**ターミナルか Finder から起動したシェルで実行してください**。他のアプリケーションに埋め込まれたターミナルからは実行しないでください。macOS はサンドボックス化されたホストから起動されたアプリにファイルダイアログを表示しません。Studio はそれを検出してパス入力（_パスを指定して開く…_、_パスを指定して新規作成…_）を代わりに提供しますが、ネイティブのダイアログが本来の方法です。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:35
msgid "What you see first"
msgstr "最初に見えるもの"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:37
msgid "Studio opens on the **project manager**: the wordmark on the left with _Start_ actions under it; _Recent_ projects on the right, and under them the _Demos_, each with a line saying what it is."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:43
msgid "_The project manager: Start actions on the left; Recent and the Demos on the right._"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:46
msgid "Action"
msgstr "操作"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:46
#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:8
msgid "What it does"
msgstr "動作"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:48
msgid "**New Project…**"
msgstr "**新規プロジェクト…**"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:48
msgid "asks for a folder name and location, creates a project there, opens the workspace"
msgstr "フォルダ名と場所を尋ね、そこにプロジェクトを作成し、ワークスペースを開く"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:49
msgid "**Open Project…**"
msgstr "**プロジェクトを開く…**"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:49
msgid "opens an existing project folder"
msgstr "既存のプロジェクトフォルダを開く"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:50
msgid "a _Demos_ row"
msgstr "_デモ_ の行"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:50
msgid "a new project that starts with a design in it: **Button → Lamp** (the design alone) and **Button → Lamp, wired** (with its devices and pins for a Raspberry Pi Pico) — [Your first board](pico-demo.md)"
msgstr "設計入りで始まる新しいプロジェクト：**Button → Lamp**（設計のみ）と **Button → Lamp, wired**（Raspberry Pi Pico 用のデバイスとピン付き）— [はじめてのボード](pico-demo.md)"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:51
msgid "a _Recent_ row"
msgstr "_最近_ の行"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:51
msgid "reopens that project; rows whose folder is gone are greyed _not found_"
msgstr "そのプロジェクトを再び開く。フォルダがなくなった行はグレーで _見つかりません_ と表示される"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:53
msgid "A **project** is a folder. Everything in it is saved as plain files ([Project files](../reference/project-files.md)): the design as `.bdl` text you can also edit in a code editor, and the canvas layout beside it. There is one kind of project; behavior groups, components and instances ([System projects](../studio/system-projects.md)) and the **Code** view ([Design, Code and Split](../studio/code-view.md)) are available in every one."
msgstr "**プロジェクト**はフォルダです。その中のすべてはプレーンなファイルとして保存されます（[プロジェクトファイル](../reference/project-files.md)）。設計はコードエディタでも編集できる `.bdl` テキストとして、その横にキャンバスのレイアウトが保存されます。プロジェクトの種類は 1 つだけで、振る舞いグループ、コンポーネント、インスタンス（[システムプロジェクト](../studio/system-projects.md)）と**コード**ビュー（[設計・コード・分割](../studio/code-view.md)）はどのプロジェクトでも使えます。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:60
msgid "The bottom line of the window shows the connection to the compiler service: _Compiler 0.1.0_ when connected, _Connecting to the compiler_ while it starts, _Compiler not connected_ if it could not. Studio does nothing semantic on its own — every check, value and verdict in the guide comes from that service — so this line is the first thing to look at if the app seems inert."
msgstr "ウィンドウの最下行はコンパイラサービスとの接続を示します。接続中は _コンパイラ 0.1.0_、起動中は _コンパイラに接続中_、失敗した場合は _コンパイラ未接続_ です。Studio は自分では意味的な処理を何もしません——ガイドのすべての検査、値、判定はそのサービスから来ます——ので、アプリが反応しないように見えたら、まずこの行を見てください。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:66
msgid "Try the finished example"
msgstr "完成した例を試す"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:68
msgid "The repository ships one complete project, `examples/smart_lamp`. _Open Project…_ → choose that folder. It is the lamp the tutorials build, with an ambient-light sensor added: two inputs, three relationships, one required output, one PWM device. You can walk its Design, Simulate and Deploy pages before building your own."
msgstr "リポジトリには完成したプロジェクトが 1 つ、`examples/smart_lamp` として同梱されています。_プロジェクトを開く…_ → そのフォルダを選びます。これはチュートリアルで作るランプに環境光センサーを加えたもので、入力 2 つ、関係 3 つ、必須出力 1 つ、PWM デバイス 1 つです。自分のものを作る前に、その設計・シミュレート・デプロイの各ページを見て回れます。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:76
msgid "[Your first behavior](first-behavior.md) — or, with a Raspberry Pi Pico at hand, [Your first board](pico-demo.md)."
msgstr "[はじめての振る舞い](first-behavior.md) — あるいは、手元に Raspberry Pi Pico があれば [はじめてのボード](pico-demo.md)。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:1
msgid "Your first board: Button → Lamp on a Raspberry Pi Pico"
msgstr "はじめてのボード：Raspberry Pi Pico でボタン → ランプ"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:3
msgid "**Goal.** Make a push button control a lamp — and run it on a real board. You will open a small product, tell Studio which pins the button and the lamp are on, build the firmware, put it on the board, and press the button."
msgstr "**目標。** 押しボタンでランプを制御し、本物のボードで動かします。小さな製品を開き、ボタンとランプがどのピンにあるかを Studio に伝え、ファームウェアをビルドし、ボードに載せ、ボタンを押します。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:7
msgid "**Time.** Fifteen minutes, plus the first build's download of the board's libraries."
msgstr "**時間。** 15 分。加えて、最初のビルドでボードのライブラリをダウンロードする時間。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:10
msgid "**Needs.** A Raspberry Pi Pico (the RP2040 board), a USB cable that carries data, one push button, two jumper wires. No LED: the demo drives the Pico's own on-board LED. Nothing to install beyond Studio and the Rust toolchain the installation page asks for ([Install and launch](install-and-launch.md))."
msgstr "**必要なもの。** Raspberry Pi Pico（RP2040 ボード）、データ通信できる USB ケーブル、押しボタン 1 個、ジャンパー線 2 本。LED は不要です。デモは Pico の基板上 LED を駆動します。Studio と、インストールページが求める Rust ツールチェーン（[インストールと起動](install-and-launch.md)）以外にインストールするものはありません。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:15
msgid "1. Wire the button"
msgstr "1. ボタンを配線する"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:17
msgid "The button goes between **GP2** and **GND**: one leg to GP2, the other to any GND pin. Nothing else. The Pico pulls the line up on its own, so the line reads low while the button is held — the demo says as much when you look at the device."
msgstr "ボタンは **GP2** と **GND** の間に付けます。片方の足を GP2 に、もう片方を任意の GND ピンに。それだけです。Pico が自分で線をプルアップするので、ボタンを押している間は線が low として読まれます——デバイスを見ればデモもそう述べています。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:22
msgid "Pico pin"
msgstr "Pico のピン"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:22
msgid "Wire"
msgstr "配線"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:24
msgid "GP2"
msgstr "GP2"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:24
msgid "one leg of the button"
msgstr "ボタンの片方の足"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:25
msgid "GND"
msgstr "GND"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:25
msgid "the other leg"
msgstr "もう片方の足"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:26
msgid "GP25"
msgstr "GP25"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:26
msgid "nothing — it is the on-board LED"
msgstr "何も付けない — 基板上の LED です"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:28
msgid "2. Open the demo"
msgstr "2. デモを開く"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:30
msgid "On the Welcome page, under **Demos**, choose **Button → Lamp, wired**. Studio asks where to put the project (it is an ordinary project: a folder with `src/main.bdl` in it) and opens it on the Design page."
msgstr "ようこそページの**デモ**で **Button → Lamp, wired** を選びます。Studio がプロジェクトの置き場所を尋ね（普通のプロジェクトです。`src/main.bdl` を含むフォルダです）、設計ページで開きます。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:36
msgid "_The demo's design: the Source pressed, the mapping block of lit that follows it, the block lit, and the lamp it drives._"
msgstr "_デモの設計：入力元 pressed、それに従う lit のマッピングブロック、ブロック lit、そしてそれが駆動するランプ。_"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:39
msgid "Three objects. **pressed** is a _Source_: a value the environment provides — the design does not say how, and the canvas shows no pin. **lit** is a relationship whose formula is simply `pressed`. **lamp** is the physical output, driven by `lit`. Nothing here is about a board; that is the next page."
msgstr "3 つのオブジェクトです。**pressed** は _入力元_：環境が与える値で、設計はその方法を述べず、キャンバスにピンはありません。**lit** は数式が単に `pressed` である関係です。**lamp** は物理出力で、`lit` に駆動されます。ここにはボードに関するものは何もありません。それは次のページです。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:44
msgid "The other demo, **Button → Lamp**, is the same design without its deployment: take it when you want to make the device choices yourself (step 3 explains them); the wired one has them made."
msgstr "もう一つのデモ **Button → Lamp** はデプロイのない同じ設計です。デバイスの選択を自分で行いたい時に選んでください（手順 3 で説明します）。wired の方は選択済みです。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:48
msgid "3. Deploy"
msgstr "3. デプロイ"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:50
msgid "Click **Deploy** (⌘3) and, in **Target**, choose **Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040)**."
msgstr "**デプロイ**（⌘3）をクリックし、**ターゲット**で **Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040)** を選びます。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:54
#: docs/user-guide/studio/deploy.md:141
msgid "_The wired demo on the Deploy page: the Pico chosen, both devices admissible and placed, and the one thing left to do — Build._"
msgstr "_デプロイページの wired デモ：Pico を選択、両デバイスとも受け入れ可能で配置済み、残る一つのこと — ビルド。_"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:57
msgid "Read the page top to bottom:"
msgstr "ページを上から下へ読みます。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:59
msgid "**Feasible on Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040).** — the devices fit the board."
msgstr "**Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040) に配置可能です。** — デバイスがボードに収まります。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:60
msgid "**Devices.** A _device_ is the piece of hardware that stands for one thing in the design. `button` is a **Digital input** for `pressed — Source`, with the **Provider** _GPIO input, active low_ (low is true: a button to ground) on pin **GP2**. `led` is a **Digital output** for `lamp`, with the **Realization** _GPIO, on/off_ on pin **GP25**. The ticks under each — for a Source _transducer · fits · placed · readable_, for an output _encoder · fits · placed_ — are the compiler's judgments; every one holds."
msgstr "**デバイス。** _デバイス_ は設計の一つのものを表すハードウェアです。`button` は `pressed — 入力元` の**デジタル入力**で、**提供方式**は _GPIO 入力、アクティブ Low_（low が真：グランドへのボタン）、ピンは **GP2**。`led` は `lamp` の**デジタル出力**で、**実現方式**は _GPIO、オン/オフ_、ピンは **GP25**。それぞれの下のチェック——入力元では _変換器 · 適合 · 配置済み · 読み取り可_、出力では _エンコーダ · 適合 · 配置済み_——はコンパイラの判断で、すべて成り立っています。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:67
msgid "**Placement.** Which pin carries what."
msgstr "**配置。** どのピンが何を担うか。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:68
msgid "**Firmware.** Where you are on the way to a running board — _✓ Deployment · **Build** · Flash · Observe_ — and the one thing to do next."
msgstr "**ファームウェア。** 動くボードへの道のりで今どこにいるか——_✓ デプロイ · **ビルド** · 書き込み · 観察_——と、次にすべき一つのこと。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:71
msgid "With the guided demo the page instead says **Not ready to build** and names the first missing thing — _pressed has no device on Raspberry Pi Pico._ — and you make the two devices: **Add device**, name it, choose its kind, choose what it is for in the third pop-up (`pressed — Source` or `lamp`), choose the Provider or Realization, type the pin. The sentence changes as you go, until it reads _Ready to build_."
msgstr "ガイド付きデモではページは代わりに**まだビルドできません**と述べ、最初に欠けているものを名指しします——_pressed には Raspberry Pi Pico 上のデバイスがありません。_——そして 2 つのデバイスをあなたが作ります。**デバイスを追加**、名前を付け、種類を選び、3 つ目のポップアップで何のためかを選び（`pressed — 入力元` または `lamp`）、提供方式または実現方式を選び、ピンを入力します。進めるにつれて文が変わり、_ビルドできます_ になります。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:78
msgid "4. Build"
msgstr "4. ビルド"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:80
msgid "Click **Build for Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040)**. The card shows what is happening — _Checking the deployment_, _Generating the crate_, _Preparing the toolchain_, _Compiling_ with the count of pieces compiled, _Writing the image_ — and ends with **Firmware built at _time_** and the image's size. The first build fetches the board's libraries and takes a few minutes; later ones take seconds. **Stop** ends a build early."
msgstr "**Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040) 向けにビルド**をクリックします。カードに進行中のことが表示され——_デプロイを確認中_、_クレートを生成中_、_ツールチェーンを準備中_、_コンパイル中_（コンパイル済みの数付き）、_イメージを書き出し中_——最後に **_時刻_ にファームウェアをビルドしました**とイメージのサイズが出ます。最初のビルドはボードのライブラリを取得するので数分かかります。以後は数秒です。**停止**でビルドを途中で終えられます。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:87
msgid "If it ends with **The build did not complete**, the card says which step and why — _The Rust target for Raspberry Pi Pico is not installed._ with the one command to run, for instance — and **Details** holds the compiler's own words. See [Troubleshooting: deployment](../troubleshooting/deployment-errors.md)."
msgstr "**ビルドは完了しませんでした**で終わったら、カードがどの段階でなぜかを述べます——例えば _Raspberry Pi Pico 向けの Rust ターゲットがインストールされていません。_ と実行すべき一つのコマンド——そして**詳細**にコンパイラ自身の言葉があります。[トラブルシューティング：デプロイ](../troubleshooting/deployment-errors.md)を参照してください。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:92
msgid "5. Flash"
msgstr "5. 書き込み"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:94
msgid "Under the built firmware the card says **No board is reachable.** and how to make one reachable: **hold the BOOTSEL button on the Pico while plugging it in** over USB. The Pico appears to the computer as a small drive named `RPI-RP2`; click **Look again** and the card names it — _Raspberry Pi Pico in BOOTSEL mode (RPI-RP2)_ — with a **Flash** button."
msgstr "ビルドされたファームウェアの下で、カードは**接続できるボードがありません。**と述べ、接続できるようにする方法を示します。**Pico の BOOTSEL ボタンを押したまま** USB で差し込みます。Pico はコンピューターに `RPI-RP2` という小さなドライブとして現れます。**再検出**をクリックすると、カードがそれを名指しし——_Raspberry Pi Pico in BOOTSEL mode (RPI-RP2)_——**書き込む**ボタンが現れます。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:102
msgid "_Built: the image is current, no board is plugged in yet, and the page says what to do._"
msgstr "_ビルド済み：イメージは最新、ボードはまだ差し込まれておらず、ページが何をすべきかを述べています。_"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:105
msgid "Click **Flash**. The image is copied onto the drive; the Pico restarts into it and the drive disappears. The card says **Flashed to Raspberry Pi Pico in BOOTSEL mode (RPI-RP2) at _time_** and then:"
msgstr "**書き込む**をクリックします。イメージがドライブにコピーされ、Pico はそれで再起動し、ドライブが消えます。カードは **_時刻_ に Raspberry Pi Pico in BOOTSEL mode (RPI-RP2) へ書き込みました**と述べ、続けて："

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:109
msgid "Try it: act on pressed; lamp should follow the design."
msgstr "試してみましょう。pressed を操作すると、lamp が設計どおりに追従するはずです。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:111
msgid "If two Picos are plugged in, the card asks which one; it never picks."
msgstr "Pico が 2 枚差し込まれていれば、カードはどちらかを尋ねます。勝手に選ぶことはありません。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:113
msgid "6. Try it"
msgstr "6. 試す"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:115
msgid "Press the button. The on-board LED lights while the button is held and goes out when you let go: `lit` is `pressed`, and `lamp` is `lit`."
msgstr "ボタンを押します。押している間は基板上の LED が点き、離すと消えます。`lit` は `pressed` で、`lamp` は `lit` です。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:118
msgid "That the flash succeeded is all Studio can tell you; whether the board behaves is yours to see. If the LED does not follow the button, check the wiring first (GP2 and GND, a button that actually closes), then [Troubleshooting: deployment](../troubleshooting/deployment-errors.md)."
msgstr "Studio が伝えられるのは書き込みが成功したことまでです。ボードが正しく振る舞うかは自分の目で確かめます。LED がボタンに追従しなければ、まず配線（GP2 と GND、実際に閉じるボタン）を確認し、次に[トラブルシューティング：デプロイ](../troubleshooting/deployment-errors.md)を見てください。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:123
msgid "7. Change it, and again"
msgstr "7. 変えて、もう一度"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:125
msgid "Change the design — make `lit` be `!pressed`, say, so the lamp is lit until you press — or the deployment — the button on GP3. The Firmware card says at once: **The firmware is from an earlier design or deployment.** and, if you had flashed, _The board runs an earlier design — build and flash again to update it._ Only **Build again** is offered; Flash comes back once the image is current. Studio never lets an old image pass for the design on screen."
msgstr "設計を変えます——例えば `lit` を `!pressed` にして、押すまでランプが点いているようにする——あるいはデプロイを変えます——ボタンを GP3 に。ファームウェアのカードはすぐに述べます。**このファームウェアは以前の設計またはデプロイのものです。**そして書き込み済みなら _ボードは以前の設計で動いています。更新するには再ビルドして書き込んでください。_ 提供されるのは**再ビルド**だけで、イメージが最新になれば書き込みが戻ります。Studio は古いイメージを画面上の設計として通すことは決してありません。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:132
msgid "What you did, in the design's terms"
msgstr "設計の言葉で言うと、何をしたのか"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:134
msgid "The design never learned about GP2 or GP25. The **Source** is what the environment provides; the **provider** — a catalogue profile, chosen on the Deploy page — is how a device reads it for the board, and the **realization** is how a device carries the output's value out. Change the board and the design stays; change the provider and the design stays. That separation is the point of the two pages ([Deploy](../studio/deploy.md))."
msgstr "設計は GP2 も GP25 も知らないままです。**入力元**は環境が与えるもの、**提供方式**——デプロイページで選ぶカタログのプロファイル——はデバイスがボードのためにそれを読む方法、**実現方式**はデバイスが出力の値を外へ運ぶ方法です。ボードを変えても設計はそのまま、提供方式を変えても設計はそのままです。その分離こそが 2 つのページの要点です（[デプロイ](../studio/deploy.md)）。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:141
msgid "Without Studio"
msgstr "Studio を使わずに"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:143
msgid "The same path from a terminal, for scripts and for checking a build without the app ([Command line](../reference/cli.md)):"
msgstr "スクリプト用に、またアプリなしでビルドを確認するために、ターミナルから同じ道をたどれます（[コマンドライン](../reference/cli.md)）。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/pico-demo.md:154
msgid "[From sensor to output](../workflows/sensor-to-output.md) extends a design with a second Source; [Deploy](../studio/deploy.md) has every state of the Firmware card."
msgstr "[センサーから出力へ](../workflows/sensor-to-output.md)は設計に 2 つ目の入力元を足します。[デプロイ](../studio/deploy.md)にはファームウェアカードのあらゆる状態があります。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:1
msgid "What is BDL?"
msgstr "BDL とは？"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:3
msgid "BDL — the Behavior Design Language — is a way of describing what a product does in terms of **what its values mean** and **how they relate**, so that a design can be checked, simulated and placed on hardware before it is programmed. Behavior Designer is the desktop tool that lets you draw, type, check and run BDL designs."
msgstr "BDL——Behavior Design Language——は、製品が何をするかを**値の意味**と**値どうしの関係**によって記述する方法です。これにより、設計はプログラミングの前に検査し、シミュレートし、ハードウェアに配置できます。Behavior Designer は BDL の設計を描き、入力し、検査し、実行するためのデスクトップツールです。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:9
msgid "This page gives you the mental model in five ideas. Each has its own page in [Concepts](../concepts/concepts.md); here they are only as big as you need them to be before the [first tutorial](first-behavior.md)."
msgstr "このページでは 5 つの考え方でメンタルモデルを示します。それぞれ [コンセプト](../concepts/concepts.md) に専用ページがあります。ここでは [最初のチュートリアル](first-behavior.md) の前に必要な分だけ説明します。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:13
msgid "1. A concept is a kind of value; a block is one such value"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:15
msgid "A lamp has a _Tilt_, a _Brightness_, maybe an _Ambient light_. Each is a **concept**: a named _kind_ of value the product senses, decides or shows — a type, and a template. A concept has a _value form_ — a quantity with a unit (an angle, a length, a temperature, or a plain number), an on/off state, or a count."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:20
msgid "The things that actually hold values are **blocks** (_Sem blocks_ in the [terminology](../reference/terminology.md)): a block is one instance of a concept in the design — `tilt`, a Tilt; `brightness`, a Brightness — and it has one value at each tick. A product may have as many blocks of one concept as it has such values: two temperature sensors are two blocks of _Temperature_. Concept : block = type : instance."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:27
msgid "Two concepts with the same value form are still different concepts. _Brightness_ and _Opacity_ may both be numbers between 0 and 1; BDL will not let you use a block of one where the other is expected, because they mean different things. This is deliberate, and it is the first thing that makes a BDL design more than a spreadsheet."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:33
msgid "2. A rule says how one value follows from others; a block's formula applies it"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:35
msgid "`dimByTilt` reads a _Tilt_ and produces a _Brightness_. That is a **rule**: a named template from some concepts to a concept, with a formula — `Tilt / 90 deg` — that is checked for units and dimensions: dividing an angle by an angle gives a plain number, which is what a brightness is. Adding an angle to a time would be refused, with the reason."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:41
msgid "A rule computes nothing by itself. A block gets its value from its own formula — `brightness = dimByTilt(tilt)` — which applies the rule to the blocks it reads; that formula is drawn on the canvas as the block's **mapping block**, joined to the blocks it reads and to the block it defines. Rule : mapping block = template : application. A block with no formula is a **Source**: its value arrives from outside (a sensor reading, a switch). In Studio a rule and a block are both created as a _relationship_ (labelled _Mapping_): one that reads something is a rule; one that reads nothing is a block."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:50
msgid "3. A design can be unfinished on purpose"
msgstr "3. 設計は意図的に未完成でいられる"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:52
msgid "You can create `dimByTilt` before you know its formula. It is then _declared_: it exists, it has a signature, and everything that depends on it can be designed around it. The tool marks it as open work, not as an error — and a block that has no formula yet is a Source, provided from outside until you say otherwise. The same goes for a concept whose value form you have not chosen yet. [Incomplete designs](../concepts/incomplete-designs.md) explains the states a design can be in and why none of them stops you working."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:60
msgid "4. Timing is explicit"
msgstr "4. タイミングは明示的"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:62
msgid "Values in a product update at different rhythms: a touch sensor at one rate, a temperature sensor at another. In BDL every value that updates on its own rhythm belongs to a named **timing domain**; a relationship that reads a value from another domain must say so and give the value to use before the first reading arrives. Memory — using last tick's value — is written into the formula, not hidden. [Timing](../concepts/timing.md) starts from the questions a designer asks and works towards the rules."
msgstr "製品内の値は異なるリズムで更新されます。タッチセンサーはあるレートで、温度センサーは別のレートで。BDL では、独自のリズムで更新されるすべての値が名前付きの**タイミングドメイン**に属します。別のドメインの値を読む関係はそう明記し、最初の読み値が届く前に使う値を与えなければなりません。記憶——前のティックの値を使うこと——は数式に書かれ、隠されません。[タイミング](../concepts/timing.md) は設計者の疑問から出発して規則へ進みます。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:70
msgid "5. Outputs are where behavior leaves the design"
msgstr "5. 出力は振る舞いが設計を離れる場所"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:72
msgid "A **physical output** — the light, the motor, the display — accepts values of one concept and is driven by exactly one block. A second block trying to drive the same output is a conflict the tool names, not a race it resolves. Which board the design will run on is a separate question: **deployment** checks whether the outputs' devices can be placed on a chosen board's pins, and never changes what the design means."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:79
msgid "Growing from a lamp to a system"
msgstr "ランプからシステムへ"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:81
msgid "Once a design has several relationships that belong together, you can **group** them into a _behavior_ — a way of organising and looking at the design that changes nothing about what it does. A behavior can be **packaged** as a reusable _component_ with an explicit boundary (what it needs, what it offers). Components are then placed as _instances_ and wired together into a _behavior system_. The [concept pages](../concepts/behavior-groups.md) take these one at a time; the [workflows](../workflows/grouping-behavior.md) walk through them on the same lamp you build in the tutorial."
msgstr "設計にまとまりのある関係がいくつかできたら、それらを _振る舞い_ として**グループ化**できます。これは設計を整理し眺める方法であり、設計が何をするかは何も変わりません。振る舞いは、明示的な境界（必要なもの、提供するもの）を持つ再利用可能な _コンポーネント_ として**パッケージ化**できます。コンポーネントは _インスタンス_ として配置され、配線されて _振る舞いシステム_ になります。[コンセプトページ](../concepts/behavior-groups.md) はこれらを 1 つずつ扱い、[ワークフロー](../workflows/grouping-behavior.md) はチュートリアルで作る同じランプで順に進めます。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:92
msgid "[Install and launch](install-and-launch.md), then [Your first behavior](first-behavior.md)."
msgstr "[インストールと起動](install-and-launch.md)、続いて [最初の振る舞い](first-behavior.md)。"

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:1
msgid "Command line"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:3
msgid "`bdld` is Studio's compiler service; it also has headless commands that read a project — flat, system or text — with the same loader Studio and the language server use, and the build and flash commands Studio's Deploy page runs through it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:8
msgid "Command"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:8
msgid "Exit code"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:10
msgid "`bdld check <project>`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:10
msgid "opens the project and prints every finding (`error[code] place: message`, with `file:line:col` for findings about the source files), then one line: name, counts, *checks, outputs complete* / *checks, outputs not yet complete* / *N error(s)*"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:10
msgid "0 no errors · 1 errors · 2 the project did not open"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:11
msgid "`bdld compile <project> [--out DIR]`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:11
msgid "generates the Rust crate into `DIR` (default `target/bdl`); refuses while the design is not ready, printing why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:11
msgid "0 written · 1 not ready · 2 did not open"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:12
msgid "`bdld compile <project> --target rp2040_pico [--tick-micros N] [--period domain=N …]`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:12
msgid "also generates the firmware for that board beside the core: every output needs a device with a realization placed on the board, and every Source a device with a provider the board can read (an unprovided Source is refused by name, `adapter.source_unprovided`); `--tick-micros` is the firmware's base tick (default 10000); build it with `cargo build --release --target thumbv6m-none-eabi --features rp2040` in `DIR`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:12
msgid "0 written · 1 refused, printing why · 2 did not open or unknown board"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:13
msgid "`bdld compile <project> --target arduino_nano …`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:13
msgid "the same for the Arduino Nano over `avr-hal`: a blocking tick loop, PWM on the board's timers, no collections; build it with `cargo +nightly-2025-04-27 build --release --target avr-none -Zbuild-std=core --features arduino_nano` in `DIR` (needs that nightly with `rust-src`, and `avr-gcc`); the exact command is in `bdl-manifest.json` under `adapter.build`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:13
msgid "as above"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:14
msgid "`bdld build <project> --target rp2040_pico`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:14
msgid "the whole path to the board's image: judges the deployment (*Checking*), writes the crate under `<project>/build/rp2040_pico/` (*Generating*; with a `rust-toolchain.toml` that pins the runtime's toolchain and the board's target, so `rustup` installs both on first use), finds cargo and the runtime crates (*Preparing*; `BDL_RUNTIME_DIR` names the repository's `runtime/` when `bdld` is not run from a checkout), runs `cargo build` printing each crate as it compiles (*Compiling*), writes the UF2 image beside the ELF (*Packaging*) and a `bdl-build.json` record with the image's fingerprint; a failure names its stage and code (`build.not_ready`, `build.toolchain_missing`, `build.target_missing`, `build.runtime_missing`, `build.cargo_failed`, `build.package_failed`) and prints the tool's words"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:14
msgid "0 built · 1 refused or failed, printing why · 2 did not open or unknown board"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:15
msgid "`bdld flash <project> --target rp2040_pico [--device ID] [--list]`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/cli.md:15
msgid "writes the last built image to the board: with `--list`, the devices reachable now and how (the Pico's bootloader drive `RPI-RP2` — hold BOOTSEL while plugging in — and, when `probe-rs` is installed, its probes); with exactly one device none need be named; with several, `--device` chooses one and nothing is written otherwise; a stale image (the project changed since the build) is refused: build again first"
msgstr ""

