msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/reference/terminology.md:8
msgid "The ladder the whole guide stands on: a **value form** is what kind of value something is; a **concept** is a named kind of value — a type, a template; a **Sem block** (a *block*) is one instance of a concept in the design; the **value at a tick** is what that block holds at one tick. Concept : Sem block = type : instance. In parallel, a **rule** is a template from concepts to a concept, and a **mapping block** is one application of rules — the formula that defines one Sem block. Rule : mapping block = template : application. The canvas draws Sem blocks, mapping blocks and outputs, joined by read, produce and drive edges; concepts and rules are templates and are not on it."
